4.4.1-stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9186) - AMD Ryzen 7 9800X3D 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 31.58 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen I used a function to assign a _default_ value for the Dictionary.get(key, default) method, I noticed that function being run, even when the _key_ existed.\n\nIt appears _default_ is being evaluated prior to the _key_ being checked, since the unexpected output precedes the expected output.\n\nI expected the implied has(_key_) operation to return false before the second argument (_default_) was evaluated.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nTry the script below. Any code added to my_function will be run, even though the get method can successfully find the key, \"Car\", in the dictionary. Note the unexpected text in the Output Dock precedes the expected output.\n\nI incrementally increased the my_function input argument to determine if the method would wait indefinitely before retrieving the key value. It appears so. At 20, the expected output was the last of 21895 lines. At 21, ERROR: [output overflow, print less text!]\n```gdscript\nextends Node\n\nvar my_dict: Dictionary = { \"Car\": 3, \"Boat\": 2, \"Airplane\": 1 }\n\n\n\nfunc print_vehicle_qty() -> void:\n\t# Unexpectedly, default calls my_function and processes code.\n\tvar quantity = my_dict.get(\"Car\", my_function(3)) # Caution! Increase input argument slowly.\n\tprint(\"Car quantity: \", quantity)\n\n\n# Arbitrary cpu burning code.\nfunc my_function(n: int) -> int:\n\tif n <= 1:\n\t\tprint(n)\n\t\treturn n\n\telse:\n\t\tprint(n)\n\t\treturn my_function(n-1) + my_function(n-2)\n\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\t\n\tprint_vehicle_qty()\n```\nOutput Dock\n```\n3\n2\n1\n0\n1\nCar quantity: 3\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116086/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116086/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}